# PyMS qinv / declared-var-unassigned fix.
# A declared real/integer referenced with no value on the reached path
# (assignment compile-time skipped: guarded by a false if() such as
# if(BULKMOD!=0)/if(ASYMMOD!=0), or behind an undefined `ifdef) is 0 in
# Verilog-A (reals zero-init). The emitter leaked the bare identifier
# instead, so the generated C++ failed to compile (K1_i, ETA0R_i, qinv,
# ...). Fix: declared-but-unassigned var -> 0 in all 3 substitution
# paths (metaprogram, C++ value, condition). Unblocks run_adms_tests decks.
# Generated 2026-09-19T09:47:18Z

diff --git a/a/ginac_emitter.py b/utils/PyMS/vae/ginac_emitter.py
